& [SourceGrounding] keeps every expansion answerable to preserved intent
  + [SG-001] Calendar and Planner are central to Cantor operation
  + [SG-002] a repository preserves snapshots and diffs of the path walked
  + [SG-003] rear attention reflects on completed work through change records
  + [SG-004] rear reflection joins forward-facing work at the same time
  + [SG-005] compiler behavior may use the same forward-and-backward shape
  + [SG-006] the source deliberately leaves calendar scope, moment cadence, repository identity, concurrency meaning, and compiler semantics unresolved
  = must: preserve the source wording, omissions, emphasis, and interpretation boundary
  = must: treat every elaboration below as derived candidate obligation until canonical SJS authority exists
  - never: alter the preserved source to make this exploded form appear original

& [SemanticRefinedCore] is one versioned temporal-semantic walk
  + [Planner] projects candidate paths through objectives, dependencies, time, resources, effects, reviews, and uncertainty
  + [Calendar] projects authorized commitments, availability, deadlines, recurrences, wake conditions, and review checkpoints through time
  + [SemanticRepository] preserves append-only material events, immutable content, snapshots, references, and declared projections
  + [ChangeCapsule] is the typed waist joining prior intent, candidate work, actual change, rear review, and admitted after-state
  + [ProspectiveLane] prepares the next candidate from an admitted version
  + [ExecutionLane] performs only separately authorized operations against a pinned version
  + [RetrospectiveLane] tests the prior transition against declared intent, evidence, and resulting meaning
  + [ObserverJoin] alone reconciles lane returns into admit, qualify, repair, branch, revert, compensate, block, or unresolved
  + [CompilerWalk] applies the same shape to forward construction and rear correspondence review
  = concise: plan forward, preserve the step, inspect backward, then release the next dependent step

& [PositiveBoundary] states what belongs
  + versioned objective, dependency, temporal, effect, and review projections
  + typed calendar items and explicit time domains
  + append-only material-event and immutable-snapshot identities
  + intent-to-actual ChangeCapsules with distinct diff surfaces
  + version-bound prospective, execution, retrospective, and Observer join states
  + fidelity-mapped Walking Attention behavior
  + forward compiler construction and rear semantic, impact, correspondence, and proof review
  + retention, sensitivity, attribution, authority, fault, replay, and deterministic fallback contracts

& [NegativeBoundary] states what remains outside
  + literal access to private chain of thought, hidden state, K/V cache, or consciousness
  + a Git commit, snapshot, or clock tick for every token or insignificant internal event
  + Calendar as autonomous user commitment or Planner as truth and authority
  + shared mutable attention state across concurrent models or lanes
  + unbounded background observation, journaling, notification, or calendar-provider access
  + rewriting prior forecasts or declared intent using hindsight
  + compiler self-certification or generated targets serving as their own independent proof
  + live desktop operation, physical calendar effects, automatic Git commits, model training, or FPGA activation

& [IdentitySet] gives each semantic job one stable name
  + [RepositoryGeneration] identifies one immutable repository policy and predecessor state
  + [TaskContractRef] identifies the governed work purpose and effect boundary
  + [PlanRevision] identifies one objective, dependency, temporal, effect, and review projection
  + [CalendarItem] identifies one proposal or commitment revision without collapsing its lifecycle
  + [TimeExpression] identifies domain, value or interval, source, zone, precision, interpretation, and uncertainty
  + [MaterialEvent] identifies one admitted observation, decision, transition, tool boundary, effect boundary, review, calendar boundary, fault, or reentry
  + [ContentObject] identifies immutable payload bytes and digest
  + [SemanticSnapshot] identifies one predecessor-bound materialized semantic state
  + [ChangeCapsule] identifies one declared transition attempt and its review lineage
  + [LaneCursor] identifies lane kind, task, input version, plan revision, review dependency, and lease or timeout
  + [ReflectionReturn] identifies one rear disposition bound to exactly one ChangeCapsule candidate generation
  + [CompilerGeneration] identifies admitted source, dependency, IR, target, proof, and policy generations
  + [LessonCandidate] identifies reviewed forecast error, plan deviation, semantic surprise, and proposed future use
  - never: use file path, line number, list position, timestamp, digest equality, or model narration as the sole identity of any semantic subject

& [RelationSet] forms the graph waist without turning proximity into proof
  + TaskContractRef has PlanRevision
  + PlanRevision proposes CalendarItem and expects ChangeCapsule
  + CalendarItem schedules or wakes TaskContractRef under exact revision and authority
  + MaterialEvent belongs_to TaskContractRef and was_recorded_in RepositoryGeneration
  + MaterialEvent references ContentObject and may materialize SemanticSnapshot
  + SemanticSnapshot derives_from zero or more exact predecessor snapshots and one admitted event frontier
  + ChangeCapsule compares before_snapshot to candidate_snapshot under declared_intent
  + ChangeCapsule attributes exact physical, semantic, behavioral, effect, calendar, support, requirement, compiler, and proof deltas
  + LaneCursor reads exact RepositoryGeneration, PlanRevision, and applicable ChangeCapsule version
  + ReflectionReturn reviews exactly one ChangeCapsule and invalidates zero or more prepared dependents
  + ObserverJoin admits at most one successor repository generation for one candidate
  + CompilerGeneration is derived_from admitted source and checked_by independently obtained proof evidence
  + LessonCandidate derives_from admitted ChangeCapsule review and is not a durable routine until separately reviewed

& [LifecycleSet] separates proposal, commitment, execution, and review
  + [PlanState] is draft, evaluated, selected, committed, executing, paused, completed, missed, cancelled, failed, or superseded
  + [CalendarState] is proposed, tentative, accepted, declined, committed, triggered, active, completed, missed, cancelled, or superseded
  + [CapsuleState] is opened, prepared, execution_requested, effect_observed, reflection_requested, reflection_returned, reconciled, admitted, rejected, reverted, compensated, or unresolved
  + [LaneState] is idle, prepared, blocked_on_authority, blocked_on_reflection, running, returned, stale, invalidated, timed_out, failed, or released
  + [CompilerState] is source_pinned, parsed, resolved, lowered, projected, rear_reviewed, reconciled, admitted, rejected, or invalidated
  = must: preserve every state transition as an event rather than rewriting the previous state
  = must: reject impossible transitions, stale generations, and lifecycle regression without an explicit corrective event

& [PlannerDepthContract] is sufficient for later canonical planning
  + [activation] is new TaskContract, changed objective, dependency, time fact, capability, effect boundary, rear return, calendar event, or wake
  + [actors] are Observer, Planner, Weaver, Honesty, Security, user or governing policy, and bounded providers
  + [data] is objective graph, dependency graph, temporal graph, effect graph, review graph, estimates, uncertainty, alternatives, and candidate schedule
  + [state] preserves draft through superseded PlanState with prior revisions immutable
  + [service_boundary] is pure projection and evaluation before any provider or physical effect adapter
  + [policy_gate] checks fact support, authority, privacy, feasibility, resource, consequence, commitment, and review requirements
  + [proof_gate] is deterministic schedule feasibility, dependency satisfaction, conflict explanation, stable normalization, and replay
  + [failure] includes false urgency, desired-state-as-fact, hidden dependency, impossible schedule, silent overcommitment, and model-only fallback failure

& [CalendarDepthContract] treats time as typed data and effects as separate authority
  + [activation] is proposal, import, invitation, response, commit, recurrence expansion, wake, reschedule, cancellation, miss, completion, or supersession
  + [actors] are owner, participant, Planner, Observer, provider adapter, notification adapter, and effect broker
  + [data] is stable item identity, revision, kind, purpose, source, authority, sensitivity, participants, TimeExpression, recurrence, dependencies, and lifecycle
  + [state] preserves proposal and commitment independently from provider synchronization
  + [service_boundary] is local versioned projection first and separately authorized provider synchronization later
  + [policy_gate] checks identity, participant authority, privacy projection, timezone policy, recurrence bounds, external effect, and notification scope
  + [proof_gate] covers timezone, daylight-saving transitions, recurrence exceptions, uncertain time, wake revalidation, miss, cancellation, and deterministic replay
  + [failure] includes time-domain collapse, stale wake, recurrence explosion, privacy leak, provider divergence, and candidate-as-commitment

& [RepositoryDepthContract] preserves the path without claiming omniscience
  + [activation] is every materially observable semantic, tool, effect, review, calendar, fault, reentry, and admission boundary
  + [actors] are Scribe, Observer, authorized adapters, retention policy, auditor, and projection exporters
  + [data] is event journal, content objects, snapshot DAG, reference indexes, task and authority attribution, retention class, and redaction lineage
  + [state] is append-only event generations plus immutable snapshots and replaceable indexes
  + [service_boundary] makes Git a human-facing projection rather than the sole repository or event authority
  + [policy_gate] checks materiality, attribution, sensitivity, retention, deletion rights, unrelated state, and content admission
  + [proof_gate] is digest verification, predecessor closure, deterministic replay, index rebuild, compaction equivalence, and unrelated-state separation
  + [failure] includes moment flood, event loss, false atomic snapshot, history rewrite, orphan payload, mixed attribution, and unauthorized retention

& [ChangeCapsuleDepthContract] makes a semantic step inspectable
  + [activation] is a declared work transition against an admitted before snapshot
  + [actors] are prospective worker, execution broker, retrospective reviewer, Observer, Scribe, Honesty, Security, Refiner, Planner, and Weaver
  + [data] is declared intent, target set, before and candidate snapshots, actual and typed semantic deltas, evidence, review, invalidation, and after snapshot
  + [state] is the CapsuleState lifecycle and one exact candidate-generation lineage
  + [service_boundary] separates preparation, physical execution, observation, review, admission, and learning
  + [policy_gate] checks source, task, target, authority, effects, unrelated changes, evidence independence, and review completeness
  + [proof_gate] is normalized capsule replay plus acceptance and negative fixtures
  + [failure] includes rear rationalization, diff-surface collapse, hidden unrelated change, missing proof, premature completion, and hindsight rewrite

& [TandemDepthContract] coordinates work without shared-state races
  + [activation] is admitted snapshot N with an open work step and a prior transition eligible for review
  + [actors] are prospective lane, execution lane, retrospective lane, Observer join, repository, timeout policy, and optional model providers
  + [data] is LaneCursor, version leases, prepared candidates, review packets, ReflectionReturn, invalidation mask, residual, and release decision
  + [state] allows preparation ahead while dependent admission and effects remain blocked at the release barrier
  + [service_boundary] is explicit versioned message exchange rather than hidden-state fusion
  + [policy_gate] checks dependency, consequence, lag allowance, rollback, provider authority, timeout, and exact version
  + [proof_gate] covers compare-and-append, stale-candidate rejection, invalidation, independent release, timeout, cancellation, crash recovery, and no deadlock
  + [failure] includes forward runaway, reflection deadlock, shared mutation, stale release, lost return, circular dependency, and false concurrency claims

& [CompilerWalkDepthContract] binds generated structures back to meaning
  + [activation] is one admitted source generation plus declared change intent and target profile
  + [actors] are parser, resolver, lowerer, projector, rear diff analyzers, proof runner, Observer, and package signer under separate authority
  + [data] is source maps, SemanticIR, loss records, target candidates, dependency and invalidation graph, correspondence results, and proof evidence
  + [state] preserves source-pinned through admitted CompilerState and never overwrites failed generations
  + [service_boundary] separates exact compilation, optional learned proposal, target toolchain, proof acquisition, and package admission
  + [policy_gate] checks supported form, identity, imports, type, effects, authority, target profile, evidence independence, and signature eligibility
  + [proof_gate] compares textual, semantic, build, behavioral, effect, correspondence, and proof diffs separately
  + [failure] includes unsupported-form erasure, source-map loss, stale dependency reuse, incomplete invalidation, target drift, and compiler self-certification

& [SubcomponentWeaveTrace] binds depth to existing Cantor fabric
  + PlannerDepthContract supports Planner temporal projection and depends_on TaskContract, faculty cycle, and semantic graph
  + CalendarDepthContract activates pertinent-history wake and constrains Operator Shell notifications and external effects
  + RepositoryDepthContract implements the durable evidence surface required by Project Narrative, pertinent history, reentry, and trusted compilation
  + ChangeCapsuleDepthContract profiles the existing SemanticTransition waist rather than creating a competing transition authority
  + TandemDepthContract refines explicit deliberation and Junction version exchange without importing shared hidden attention
  + CompilerWalkDepthContract constrains the multi-target compiler purpose and leaves target-specific ABI and toolchain authority downstream
  + each accepted relation is source- or assessment-grounded; naming resemblance alone creates no weave edge

& [ConstraintLedger] is source-grounded and persistent
  + [C-001] preserved source remains immutable and separately hashed
  + [C-002] no canonical, implementation, provider, background, effect, training, or import authority is inferred
  + [C-003] Planner proposes paths and never establishes truth, priority, commitment, or effect authority by convenience
  + [C-004] Calendar distinguishes proposal, commitment, execution, miss, cancellation, and supersession
  + [C-005] civil, instant, monotonic, logical, valid, transaction, and uncertain time remain distinct
  + [C-006] time claims carry source, zone, precision, interpretation, and uncertainty
  + [C-007] every durable record is attributable to exact task, source, authority, repository generation, and conversation or process where applicable
  + [C-008] event position, timestamp, digest equality, and textual order do not alone prove causality or semantic identity
  + [C-009] Git is a projection; automatic commit is not required for micro-events or ordinary semantic events
  + [C-010] source, physical, semantic, behavioral, effect, calendar, build, correspondence, and proof diffs remain distinct
  + [C-011] prepared-ahead work cannot commit dependent effects or admission before applicable rear review
  + [C-012] each lane reads immutable versions and joins through compare-and-append or an equivalent atomic version check
  + [C-013] prior intent, forecasts, plans, diffs, and reviews are never rewritten to match hindsight
  + [C-014] unrelated dirty or external state remains separate from attributed work
  + [C-015] provider output and generated artifacts are untrusted candidates until independent gates admit them
  + [C-016] privacy, sensitivity, retention, redaction, deletion, and external projection remain explicit
  + [C-017] deterministic exact fallback remains available when Planner, rear model, calendar provider, or learned router is absent
  + [C-018] Walking Attention behavior is imported only through digest-pinned fidelity mapping and explicit exclusions
  + [C-019] ChangeCapsule remains a profile over existing semantic transition authority rather than a parallel state engine
  + [C-020] compiler admission requires Observer reconciliation and separately obtained proof evidence

& [ExpandedObligationSet] deepens CTPR-001 through CTPR-038
  + [CTPR-X01] every planned step binds TaskContract, PlanRevision, repository generation, Calendar revision, expected ChangeCapsule, and review dependency
  + [CTPR-X02] every wake revalidates purpose, assumptions, authority, target existence, dependency state, sensitivity, and present relevance before release
  + [CTPR-X03] every time expression declares its domain and rejects conversion without explicit policy
  + [CTPR-X04] recurrence expansion is bounded by horizon, count, or governing query and preserves exceptions as revisions
  + [CTPR-X05] materiality policy classifies semantic, tool, effect, review, calendar, fault, reentry, and micro-event boundaries
  + [CTPR-X06] retention policy defines transient, durable, compacted, redacted, archived, and deletion-requested states
  + [CTPR-X07] snapshot creation declares observed scope and never claims atomicity beyond the acquisition contract
  + [CTPR-X08] ChangeCapsule declares target and unrelated sets before attributing actual changes
  + [CTPR-X09] rear review compares declared intent with independently observed deltas and may refuse completion
  + [CTPR-X10] reflection return binds one candidate generation and cannot release a different generation
  + [CTPR-X11] invalidation propagates through exact dependency edges and records why each prepared artifact was retained, remasked, or discarded
  + [CTPR-X12] bounded lag declares maximum dependent distance, consequence ceiling, rollback contract, timeout, and residual handling
  + [CTPR-X13] crash recovery reconstructs lane and capsule state from durable versions without replaying an effect by assumption
  + [CTPR-X14] provider absence selects deterministic projection or explicit unavailable status rather than silently changing semantics
  + [CTPR-X15] Walking Attention import records source commit, file digests, mapped behavior, changed behavior, and excluded behavior
  + [CTPR-X16] compiler rear impact identifies all invalidated IR, indexes, packages, schedules, workflows, tools, models, and hardware projections reachable from changed semantics
  + [CTPR-X17] correspondence evidence derives from source maps, target inspection, fixtures, and external observations rather than the generated target's assertion
  + [CTPR-X18] a lesson remains a candidate until review establishes supported scope, invalidation condition, and safe future application
  + [CTPR-X19] user-visible calendars and reports distinguish forecast, actual, deviation, review status, and current commitment
  + [CTPR-X20] external calendar, notification, Git, desktop, model, training, or hardware effects require separate capabilities and auditable grants
  + [CTPR-X21] every rejection, timeout, invalidation, compensation, and unresolved disposition preserves a bounded reentry record
  + [CTPR-X22] normalized replay produces the same plan ordering, capsule lineage, join decisions, and admitted final state for the deterministic profile

& [RequirementCoverage] keeps the assessment set visible
  + [CTPR-001_to_CTPR-008] are covered by SemanticRefinedCore, IdentitySet, LifecycleSet, PlannerDepthContract, and CalendarDepthContract
  + [CTPR-009_to_CTPR-014] are covered by RepositoryDepthContract, RelationSet, CaptureCadencePolicy, and ChangeCapsuleDepthContract
  + [CTPR-015_to_CTPR-021] are covered by WalkingAttentionFidelityBoundary, TandemDepthContract, and JoinProtocol
  + [CTPR-022_to_CTPR-028] are covered by CompilerWalkDepthContract, DiffTaxonomy, and LearningBoundary
  + [CTPR-029_to_CTPR-032] are covered by CalendarRepositoryJoin, ConstraintLedger, and ExpandedObligationSet
  + [CTPR-033_to_CTPR-038] are covered by DeterministicFirstProof, QualityMeasures, NegativeProofSet, and AuthorityBoundary

& [CaptureCadencePolicy] resolves every moment as material semantic change
  + [always_durable] is semantic transition, tool request and result, effect authorization and observation, review disposition, calendar commitment change, fault, yield, reentry, and admission
  + [conditionally_durable] is progress, retrieval, model proposal, telemetry, and diagnostic observation when policy, fault analysis, liveness, or proof needs them
  + [normally_transient] is token production, repeated unchanged polling, renderer frames, and internal model narration
  + [materiality_test] asks whether omission would alter replay, attribution, authority, consequence, proof, fault diagnosis, or faithful reentry
  + [compaction_rule] retains source range, digest, omitted count, policy, and equivalence proof
  - never: use archive volume as a proxy for thoughtfulness

& [WalkingAttentionFidelityBoundary] is digest-pinned candidate import
  + [observed_repository_commit] is 35d24b9245dbf1625dd20e29860e943981f65300
  + [observed_repository_branch] is codex/walking-attention-pulse
  + [excluded_dirty_entry_count] is 584
