  + [Rear_Reflection_Frame_sha256] is 5E3746DDDB5D008E9EE8009D50671607982D5D1EF55CCEC96BB0FE29EDC4CE4D
  + [Walking_Attention_Tandem_Exchange_sha256] is 5E34D5E0FD2EA979077109BE47F25CA4C1816EB8EC3F45B112C9144007FBB267
  + [Tandem_Authority_sha256] is 898ADDB7F4E43969A4331C54453D77DACE327AA549C675A718B9E45C76E26B40
  + [forward_mapping] AttentionContinuityFrame becomes a ProspectiveFrame over exact admitted versions
  + [rear_mapping] RearReflectionRecord becomes a version-bound ChangeCapsule review
  + [tandem_mapping] forward commit, reflection request, return, reconciliation, and next release become LaneState transitions
  + [reentry_mapping] NextReentryMessage becomes revised Planner and Calendar continuation state
  + [excluded] is private chain of thought, consciousness claims, hidden attention, fixed pulse timing, and unrestricted executor authority
  = must: reverify repository commit, status, byte lengths, and digests before any canonical import

& [JoinProtocol] is a versioned release barrier
  + prospective preparation reads admitted N and may prepare independent or reversible candidate work
  + execution requires exact target generation and separate effect authority
  + retrospective review reads N-minus-1, N, prior declared intent, observed deltas, and proof
  + join compares lane task, purpose, repository generation, plan revision, capsule generation, and review dependency
  + invalidating review remasks or discards every dependent prepared artifact through recorded dependency edges
  + non-dependent prepared material may survive only when its premises remain exact and Observer records that determination
  + timeout yields explicit residual and policy disposition; it never fabricates approval
  + release appends one successor state or fails stale without mutating the admitted head

& [DiffTaxonomy] prevents false equivalence
  + [textual_diff] is byte, token, file, and source-span change
  + [physical_diff] is observed filesystem, process, network, calendar-provider, device, or external-system change
  + [semantic_diff] is identity, meaning, relation, clause, contract, authority, uncertainty, lifecycle, and effect change
  + [behavioral_diff] is observable input-to-output and state-transition change
  + [build_diff] is IR, index, package, dependency, toolchain, and target artifact change
  + [calendar_diff] is estimate, commitment, trigger, recurrence, miss, cancellation, and completion change
  + [proof_diff] is requirement coverage, evidence, test, confidence, contradiction, and residual change
  = must: record explicit cross-surface correspondence rather than assuming one diff implies another

& [CalendarRepositoryJoin] connects forecast to observed history
  + schedule entries point to exact task, plan, repository, expected capsule, and review identities
  + actual work appends observations without replacing the scheduled record
  + missed and cancelled work preserve reason, authority, and subsequent disposition
  + rear review may propose estimate, dependency, recurrence, risk, or review-policy revisions
  + Planner uses only admitted revisions for future uncommitted candidate paths
  + external synchronization remains a separately authorized and independently reconciled projection

& [LearningBoundary] keeps reflection corrigible
  + forecast error, plan deviation, semantic surprise, proof failure, and user correction may form LessonCandidate records
  + each candidate states source capsules, scope, counterexample, invalidation condition, confidence, and proposed use
  + Honesty guards evidential attribution and Security guards authority, privacy, and consequence boundaries
  + Observer admission may update a routine candidate, retrieval weight, evaluation corpus, or planning prior under separate governing authority
  + history remains unchanged even when future policy learns from it
  - never: convert rear narration directly into SOP authority, model training data, or routing weight

& [FaultSet] is explicit and fail-closed
  + calendar_as_plan
  + false_urgency
  + time_domain_collapse
  + stale_wake
  + recurrence_explosion
  + calendar_privacy_leak
  + provider_projection_divergence
  + moment_flood
  + event_loss_or_orphan_content
  + snapshot_overclaim
  + history_rewrite
  + rear_rationalization
  + diff_surface_collapse
  + unrelated_diff_mix
  + forward_runaway
  + reflection_deadlock
  + shared_mutation_race
  + stale_or_wrong_generation_release
  + incomplete_invalidation
  + compiler_self_certification
  + unsupported_form_erasure
  + source_map_or_correspondence_loss
  + unauthorized_external_effect
  + learned_lesson_scope_escape

& [DeterministicFirstProof] is the smallest implementation-facing frontier after later authority
  + one logical clock with explicit civil-time conversion examples and no live clock dependency
  + one fake Calendar with availability, deadline, review checkpoint, and bounded recurrence
  + one objective decomposed into three dependent steps and one reversible simulated effect
  + one prospective path with a deliberate execution deviation and one prepared dependent step
  + one append-only fake repository with normalized material events and immutable snapshots
  + one rear review that detects deviation and a newly exposed requirement, then refuses premature completion
  + one join that invalidates the prepared dependent, replans, and releases the corrected next step
  + one bounded SOP change compiled through textual, semantic, impact, target-correspondence, and proof review
  + one replay that reproduces normalized schedules, capsules, dispositions, invalidations, and admitted state
  + zero live calendar, background listener, real concurrent model, automatic Git commit, physical desktop, training, or hardware effect

& [NegativeProofSet] rejects attractive false shortcuts
  + stale repository, plan, calendar, capsule, lane, or compiler generation
  + unsourced, zoneless, falsely precise, or domain-collapsed time
  + candidate schedule presented as user commitment
  + one unrelated file or external change mixed into attributed work
  + missing, late, duplicated, or wrong-generation reflection
  + forward admission while an applicable rear gate is pending
  + sequential observation described as an atomic world snapshot
  + modified historical intent or forecast
  + generated target cited as its own independent proof
  + provider absence silently changing semantics instead of selecting exact fallback

& [QualityMeasures] test useful thoughtfulness
  + [planning] dependency satisfaction, feasibility, deadline fit, slack, uncertainty, alternatives, and correction rate
  + [calendar] timezone, recurrence, commitment, wake, miss, cancellation, reschedule, and provider-reconciliation correctness
  + [reflection] overreach, underreach, missing-proof and requirement detection plus false-positive rate
  + [diff] identity, relation, contract, authority, effect, schedule, target-impact precision and recall
  + [join] stale rejection, invalidation completeness, release correctness, bounded lag, crash recovery, deadlock absence, and replay
  + [history] event completeness, attribution, unrelated-state separation, compaction fidelity, privacy, and inspectability
  + [cost] journal volume, snapshot amplification, review latency, blocked forward time, compiler work, storage, and user attention

& [SevenFoldTrace] records constrained expansion and pruning
  + [fold_1_subject] identity and boundary
  + [fold_1_edge_probe] Calendar_display_to_temporal_authority_surface and repository_as_Git_to_semantic_event_DAG
  + [fold_1_gain_delta] stable identities for the Planner, Calendar, repository, ChangeCapsule, three lanes, Observer join, and compiler walk
  + [fold_1_pruned_material] Calendar_as_UI_only, Planner_as_authority, Git_as_runtime_truth, and reflection_as_hidden_chain_of_thought
  + [fold_1_frontier] typed data and relation cardinality
